   "text": "The drawing matches vinblastine: a catharanthine-derived nine-membered-ring indole half joined to a vindoline half.\n\n- **Left half:** a C(Et)(OH) centre sits in a bridged azacycle. A bridgehead CH has a hashed H. A quaternary carbon bears a wedged CO2Me and links the indole (NH, fused benzene, CH2CH2N chain) to the aryl ring of the right half.\n- **Right half:** the aryl ring carries an OMe next to the linking carbon and is fused to an N-methyl indoline. The attached cage has a tertiary amine, a CH=CH alkene, a quaternary C(Et), a CH\u2013OAc, and a C(OH)(CO2Me).\n\nI did not derive the stereo marks independently from the wedges and hashes. I took the stereodescriptors from the known vinblastine SMILES, which I recalled from memory, because the drawn connectivity and wedge pattern agree with that molecule.\n\nSMILES: CC[C@@]1(C[C@H]2C[C@@](C3=C(CCN(C2)C1)C4=CC=CC=C4N3)(C5=C(C=C6C(=C5)[C@]78CCN9[C@H]7[C@@](C=CC9)([C@H]([C@@]([C@@H]8N6C)(C(=O)OC)O)OC(=O)C)CC)OC)C(=O)OC)O"
